# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Platform Designer / IP generated output. Only the .qsys/.ip source files
# need to be tracked - `quartus_ipgenerate <project> -c <revision>` (or the
# full `quartus_sh --flow compile <project> -c <revision>`, after generating
# the project with `quartus_sh -t build_de25_nano_uart.tcl`) regenerates all
# of this from the .qsys/.ip files alone. Verified 2026-09-10: deleted these
# directories, ran quartus_ipgenerate, and every regenerated file (down to
# hps_subsys_bb.v/agilex_hps_bb.v/emif_io96b_hps_bb.v) came back byte-for-byte
# identical to what was previously committed by hand; a full
# `quartus_sh --flow compile` also succeeded end-to-end from that clean
# state. This superseded an earlier, overly-conservative assumption (see
# hps/README.md's "Platform Designer Generic Component limitation") that
# ALL generated output needed to be checked in - that limitation is real
# but narrower: it's about *editing* an .ip file's parameters (e.g.
# reconfiguring an interface's export mode) requiring the GUI once, not
# about generating output from an already-configured .ip/.qsys file, which
# is fully scriptable.
hps/hps_subsys/
hps/ip/hps_subsys/agilex_hps/
hps/ip/hps_subsys/hps_subsys_s10_user_rst_clkgate_0/
hps/ip/qsys_top/emif_io96b_hps/
hps/**/*.qpf
hps/**/*.qsf

# bare-metal HPS test build output (see hps/baremetal_uart1_test/README.md
# and hps/baremetal_lwh2f_regs/README.md)
hps/baremetal_uart1_test/build/
hps/baremetal_lwh2f_regs/build/
# hps/baremetal-drivers is a `git clone` per that README (or, locally, a
# symlink to one) - no trailing slash so this also matches the symlink case
# (a trailing slash would only match a real directory, not a symlink to one).
hps/baremetal-drivers

# leftover Quartus project working directory from an earlier local run -
# output_files/ above already covers the normal case; this project's own
# build/ happened to use a differently-named directory once.
/build/

# linux/build_de25_nano_linux.sh output (ATF/U-Boot/kernel/rootfs build
# tree) and linux/make_jic.sh output (the combined SPL+bitstream QSPI
# image) - both fully reproducible from linux/ scripts, shouldn't be
# committed. This was previously untracked only by omission, not by an
# actual .gitignore rule - a 16.7 MB .jic sat unignored in here.
linux/build_output/
